# What does NOT go into the .vsix.
#
# vsce packages the directory holding this manifest, so the monorepo's other workspaces are already
# outside it. The entries for benchmarks, results and .vscode-test are deliberate anyway: a relative
# path or a future restructure must not be able to pull fifteen fixture repositories and hours of
# run journals into a published extension.
#
# The shape is "exclude broadly, then re-include exactly what ships", so a new directory is left out
# by default rather than included by omission.

# Everything, then the exceptions below.
**

# --- What actually ships -----------------------------------------------------
#
# Listed by exact type rather than by directory. A negation wins over any later exclusion in vsce,
# whatever the order, so `!dist/webview/**` followed by `dist/**/*.map` still ships the maps — which
# is how 1.25 MB of source maps got into the first attempt at this package. Naming the extensions
# that ship is the only form of this list that cannot be overridden by accident.
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE.md
!resources/*.png
!dist/extension.js
!dist/webview/.vite/manifest.json
!dist/webview/assets/*.js
!dist/webview/assets/*.css
!server/index.js

# --- Never, at any path ------------------------------------------------------
# Earlier packages live beside this manifest; six of them would otherwise be packaged into the
# seventh.
**/*.vsix
**/.vscode-test/**
**/node_modules/**
**/benchmarks/**
**/results/**
**/tests/**
**/src/**
**/*.ts
**/*.tsx
**/tsconfig*.json
**/tsup.config.*
**/.eslintrc*
**/eslint.config.*
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.git/**
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
